      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Soil erosion involves removal and movement of soil by agents such as water or wind. Clearing vegetation, leaving ground bare or disturbing soil can increase exposure. Plant cover intercepts some rain, roots help bind soil and roughness can slow runoff. When these protections decline, raindrop impact and flowing water can detach and carry material more readily. The effect depends on slope, rainfall intensity, soil properties and the length of time the ground remains unprotected.",
      "claim_ids": [
