      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-03",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Loss of topsoil can reduce rooting depth, organic matter and nutrient reserves, making later production harder. Sediment can also accumulate in channels or reservoirs, affecting water storage and aquatic habitats. This links an on-farm effect to downstream consequences. Erosion is not the same as soil becoming infertile through nutrient removal in a harvested crop, although both processes can reduce nutrient availability. State the mechanism supported by the resource.",
