      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Carrying capacity is conditional rather than a permanent fixed animal count. The forage available after good rains differs from that during a prolonged dry period. Stocking decisions should respond to resource condition and expected recovery, not simply the area within a fence. Water provision also changes grazing distribution: a new point can spread use but may increase pressure nearby or support more animals if stocking rises. Judge the actual pattern of use and recovery.",
      "claim_ids": [
