    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Bush management can create its own damage if heavy equipment disturbs soil, useful species are removed or bare ground remains exposed. The product obtained from removed biomass also has transport and processing requirements. A saleable biomass output is an economic benefit, but it does not prove that rangeland condition improved. Compare grass recovery, cover, erosion and relevant biodiversity with the stated management objective over an appropriate period.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-2",
