    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Pesticides can affect non-target organisms if exposure occurs, while unsuitable storage or handling can create risks beyond the target field. Effects depend on substance, dose, route and conditions. Manure can also contribute nutrients, pathogens or oxygen-demanding material when badly managed. The organic origin of a material does not remove the need for suitable storage, placement and quantities. Agricultural pollution should therefore be assessed through actual pathways and effects rather than a simple natural-versus-chemical distinction.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-2",
