    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-15",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Consider a hypothetical farm record. After a field is left bare on a slope, a storm produces sediment-rich runoff and a lower reservoir becomes silted. This supports a cover-to-runoff-to-sediment pathway. A separate irrigated plot shows rising soil salt measurements over repeated seasons with poor drainage. That supports salinisation, not proof that the first field's sediment came from salt. Matching observations to processes prevents an answer from combining unrelated environmental labels.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-2",
