    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-16",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Environmental effects can reduce later livelihoods as well as current ecosystem condition. Eroded soil, poor grazing or degraded water may increase costs or lower future output. Sustainable management therefore concerns the continuity of useful production and ecological functions. A strategy must be judged by observed resource condition and human needs over time; short-term output alone cannot establish that the productive base has been maintained.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-2",
