    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "For example, plot A has 80% ground cover before heavy use and 40% afterwards; a matched plot B changes from 80% to 75% over the same interval. The first decline is larger, but attributing the whole difference to grazing still requires information about soils, rainfall and other disturbance. The record supports a cover contrast. If runoff and sediment observations are also available, they can strengthen a proposed erosion pathway. Evidence should be combined through the mechanism, rather than allowing one percentage to establish every environmental consequence.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-2",
