    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-19",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Management outcomes should be assessed beyond the visible intervention. Installing a drainage ditch is an action; a lower harmful water table or reduced root-zone salt concentration is an outcome requiring observations. Thinning bush is an action; recovery of suitable grass cover and reduced erosion require follow-up. Applying a pesticide is an action; reduced crop damage and limited non-target effects require relevant evidence. This distinction prevents an environmental evaluation from confusing expenditure or activity with successful resource protection.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.12-01-1",
