    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.12-20",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Environmental costs may fall outside the farm's own accounts. Sediment or nutrients entering shared water can affect other users even if the producing farm earns a return. A judgement of sustainability therefore needs a wider boundary than the enterprise's immediate revenue. It can recognise employment and food production while still requiring improvements in soil retention, water quality or recovery.",
